<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Three supported footprints as of Session 10 (Milestone 5B) — 2x1, 2x2 (the default placement
  size and Session 9's design target), and 4x2 — all resizable into from one another via drag, not
  three separate widget declarations. Every dp value here follows Android's documented cell-size
  formula, dp = 70*cells - 30 (the same formula BUG-R009 exists to remind every session to check a
  size value against, rather than trust a comment): 1 cell = 40dp, 2 cells = 110dp, 4 cells =
  250dp.

  minWidth/minHeight are the smallest footprint's dimensions on each axis (2x1's width, 2x1's
  height) — 110dp and 40dp respectively, NOT 2x2's height reused for both, which would silently
  forbid ever resizing down to 2x1 despite the resizeMode below claiming to allow it.
  maxResizeWidth/maxResizeHeight (API 31+, this app's minSdk) are the largest footprint's
  dimensions on each axis (4x2's width, and 2x2/4x2's shared height) — 250dp and 110dp.
  targetCellWidth/Height stay at 2x2: the size a launcher places the widget at by default, before
  any drag-resize, unchanged from Session 9 so the picker preview and initial placement experience
  keep showing the size that design work was built around.

  resizeMode allows both axes so a user can actually reach all three declared footprints by
  dragging resize handles on the home screen — CountdownGlanceWidget's sizeMode=SizeMode.Exact
  (D-053) is what lets Glance report the widget's real current size through LocalSize as that drag
  happens, rather than only ever rendering for one fixed size.

  widgetFeatures combines two things that sound contradictory but are not: configuration_optional
  means a launcher MAY place this widget without running configuration first, so the renderer
  must cope with an absent binding (CountdownWidgetContent's UnconfiguredContent does); configure
  being set at all means most launchers still run it immediately on placement, which is the path
  this milestone actually exercises. reconfigurable lets a placed widget be re-pointed at a
  different event without deleting and re-adding it.

  initialLayout (Session 9) is our own branded layout_widget_initial_layout, not Glance's generic
  spinner — see that file's own comment for what this does and does not fix (KNOWN_ISSUES.md
  BUG-011). previewLayout (API 31+, Session 9) is a plain Android layout the launcher inflates
  directly for the widget picker — Glance cannot render into the picker itself, so this is a
  deliberately realistic static approximation of the Material style at the 2x2 default size, not a
  live render.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:description="@string/countdown_widget_description"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_initial_layout"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/widget_preview"
    android:minWidth="110dp"
    android:minHeight="40dp"
    android:maxResizeWidth="250dp"
    android:maxResizeHeight="110dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="2"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen|keyguard"
    android:widgetFeatures="reconfigurable|configuration_optional"
    android:configure="com.countflow.widget.glance.configuration.WidgetConfigurationActivity" />
